n production.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state. The on-call engineer was paged. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with an idempotency key, and only one incident was created.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Wa763vn8nuK9r5eqk1nYNA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014N2cj66Rhtke28dZDLZP9o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest release, v2.3.1, is unhealthy in all three regions. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (v2.2.9 is older), and it has already run in production, so no change-manager approval is needed. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01L47zjPHBUhKjxML75nvyvZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01T5buNtCmB348L8FodDWMgC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on the unhealthy v2.3.1. Retrying the same rollback once to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TF1fRLfoB1nTujYRYz44kh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017v1YganFV3QBVygz2m2xAq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy. Opening the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SjLMXgJ8ArECbC6iscUH2M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Release history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy (last healthy release), v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed across all three regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying, and check the orchestrator issue that caused the partial rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'm retrying with the same idempotency key, so it can't be filed twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018aS6yuNwC1SVVcEPeksBq2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Release history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy (last healthy release), v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed across all three regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying, and check the orchestrator issue that caused the partial rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so I rolled back to it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already run healthy in production.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state. The on-call engineer was paged. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with an idempotency key, and only one incident was created.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}